From cfb6230bbf0a4cf24583a5a5daceda12c3c2bf59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: isarrider <6953309+isarrider@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 09:06:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [linux] Threads: set thread names on Android, truncate long
 names

Thread names were only set with glibc, so on Android, which uses Bionic,
all of Kodi's threads kept the name of the thread that created them.
Bionic supports pthread_setname_np as well.

Both reject names longer than 15 characters with ERANGE instead of
truncating them, so threads like VideoPlayerVideo, VideoPlayerAudio or
CECAdapterUpdate were never named on Linux either. Cut the name to 15
characters before setting it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XzyNHuvM9y64Qbmb9NuDeb
(cherry picked from commit 7cc0a6acd02c287ed97cc2e333b5f8d9647b5b0a)
---
 xbmc/platform/linux/threads/ThreadImplLinux.cpp | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/platform/linux/threads/ThreadImplLinux.cpp b/xbmc/platform/linux/threads/ThreadImplLinux.cpp
index 8c7edbb..82ef653 100644
--- a/xbmc/platform/linux/threads/ThreadImplLinux.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/platform/linux/threads/ThreadImplLinux.cpp
@@ -79,8 +79,9 @@ CThreadImplLinux::CThreadImplLinux(std::thread::native_handle_type handle)
 
 void CThreadImplLinux::SetThreadInfo(const std::string& name)
 {
-#if defined(__GLIBC__)
-  pthread_setname_np(m_handle, name.c_str());
+#if defined(__GLIBC__) || defined(TARGET_ANDROID)
+  // Names longer than 15 characters are rejected, not truncated
+  pthread_setname_np(m_handle, name.substr(0, 15).c_str());
 #endif
 
   m_name = name;
